{{also|Bask|bäsk}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en|bask (disambiguation)|bask}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰeh₁-}}
From {{der|en|non|baðask|t=to take a bath|lit=to bathe oneself}}, [[mediopassive]] form from underlying {{m|non|baða|t=to bathe}} + {{m|non|sik|t=oneself}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*baþōną}} and {{m|gem-pro|*sek}}. Doublet of {{cog|en|bathe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|bäsk|a=RP}} {{IPA|en|/bɑːsk/}}
* {{enPR|băsk|a=GA}} {{IPA|en|/bæsk/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-bask.ogg|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|Basque|basque}} (in some dialects)
* {{rhymes|en|æsk|ɑːsk|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To bathe in warmth; to be exposed to pleasant heat.
#: {{co|en|to '''bask''' in the sun}}
#* {{RQ:Goldsmith Traveller|page=5|passage=The naked Negro, panting at the line, / '''Baſks''' in the glare, or ſtems the tepid wave, / And thanks his Gods for all the good they gave.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 October 20|author=Paul Stephen|title=Leisure and Pleasure on the Far North Line|journal=RAIL|issue=942|page=48|text=There will be no problems with visibility, or the highly changeable Highland weather, as Scotland '''basks''' in what is reported to be the country's hottest September day for more than a century.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To take great pleasure or satisfaction; to feel warmth or happiness. (Usually followed by "in".)
#: {{co|en|to '''bask''' in someone’s favour}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''basked''' in her love.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=November 7, 2012|author=Matt Bai|title=Winning a Second Term, Obama Will Confront Familiar Headwinds|work=New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/in-president-obamas-second-term-familiar-challenges.html?pagewanted=all&_r=0| passage=As President Obama turns his attention once again to filling out a cabinet and writing an Inaugural Address, this much is clear: he should not expect to '''bask''' in a surge of national unity, or to witness a crowd of millions overrun the Mall just to say they were there.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 10, 2011|author=Alistair Magowan|title=Aston Villa 1 - 0 Newcastle| work=BBC Sport| url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9446263.stm| passage=On this evidence they will certainly face tougher tests, as a depleted Newcastle side seemed to '''bask''' in the relative security of being ninth in the table}}

